hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"816","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Wala' is a relation like the relation of descent, which cannot be sold or given.\""
"817","Hazrat Abu Qalaba narrates from Hazrat Anas that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The most knowledgeable of you is Zayd bin Thabit (may God be pleased with him) who is an expert on inheritance.\""
"818","On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is not proper for a Muslim to intend to make a will about something he owns, but he spends two nights in a state where he does not have a written will.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"819","On the authority of Hazrat Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he says: I said: O Messenger of Allah! I am a wealthy man and my only heir is my daughter. So should I give two-thirds of the wealth in charity? He said: \"No.\" I asked again: Shall I give half of my wealth in charity? He said: \"No.\" I asked for the third time: So can I give one-third of my wealth in charity? He said: \"Yes! But one third is too much. It is better for you to leave your heirs rich than to leave them needy and to spread their hands in front of the people.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"820","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that a person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! My mother died suddenly and left no will. My opinion about her is that if she had a conversation, she would (definitely) give charity. Will he be rewarded if I give charity on his behalf? He said: \"Yes.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) These words are from Muslim."
"821","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Umamah Bahli (may God be pleased with him) that I heard the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace) say: “Allah has given every rightful person his right, so there is no will for an heir.” What is the hadith from and this addition has also been quoted at the end of it: \"Unless his heirs wish.\""
"822","On the authority of Hazrat Muadh bin Jabal, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah has favored you by allowing you to bequeath one-third of your wealth at the time of death, so that your good deeds may increase.\" Allah knows best."
"823","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is entrusted with something, there is no responsibility on him.” (Narrated by Ibn Majah and its chain of transmission is weak.)"
"824","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “O community of youth! Whoever among you can afford to marry should do so, because marriage is very attractive and protects the private parts. And whoever cannot afford it, he should fast, because it (fasting) crushes his desires.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"825","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) praised Allah and said: \"But I pray (at night) and I sleep (Nafli) I fast and I break it and I also marry women. So whoever turns away from my Sunnah has nothing to do with me.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"826","It is narrated from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, ordered marriage and strictly forbade celibacy and said: \"Marry women who are very loving, who bear many children, because I will be proud of other prophets on the Day of Judgment because of your abundance.\" It is narrated on the authority of Muaqal bin Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"827","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman is married for four reasons: because of her wealth, because of her family, because of her beauty, and because of her religion.” So get success through the pious. Both your hands are dusty.” (Al-Bukhari and Muslim and the rest of the seven also narrated it.)"
"828","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) congratulated a person on his marriage, he would say: “May Allah bless you and bless you and both of you.” (It is narrated by Ahmad and the four, as well as by Tirmidhi, Ibn Khuzimah and Ibn Hibban, and it is authentic.)"
"829","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us this tashahhud in times of need: are taken We praise Him, we seek His help, we seek His forgiveness. And they seek refuge in Allah from the evil of their souls. Whomever Allah guides, there is no one to mislead, and whomever Allah leads astray, there is no one to guide. And I bear witness that there is no (true) god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is His servant and Messenger.” And then he recited three verses. (It was narrated by Ahmad and the four. Tirmidhi and Hakim called it Hasan.)"
"830","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When one of you proposes marriage to a woman, if it is possible for him to see that thing (goodness, beauty, beauty, etc.) in her that would lead to marriage for him, then he should do so.\" And the tradition of Muhammad bin Muslimah is witnessed in Ibn Majah and Ibn Hibban.)"
"831","It is narrated in Sahih Muslim on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to a man who wanted to marry a woman: \"Have you seen her?\" He said: No. He said: \"Go and see it.\""
"832","On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should give a message of marriage upon the message of marriage of his brother, until the person who gave the message of marriage voluntarily abandons it or the person who gave the message of marriage gives permission to him.” (Bukhari and Muslim – these words are from Bukhari)."
"833","It was narrated from Hazrat Sahl bin Saad Sa'idi, may Allah be pleased with him, that a woman came to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have come to sacrifice myself for you.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him. 'First upwards, then downwards.' When the woman saw that you had not made a decision about her, she sat down. Meanwhile, a companion stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! If you don't need this woman, marry her to me. He asked him: \"Do you have anything?\" He said: O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! Nothing. He said: \"Go to your house and search if you find anything?\" So he left, then came back and said: By Allah! I didn't find anything. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again said: \"Search\" even if it is an iron ring. The man then went again and came back and said: O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! Even an iron ring is not available. But this is a cloak of mine (Hazrat Sahl, may Allah be pleased with him) says that he did not have an upper cloak. ) Half of it I will give to him. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"What will this (woman) do with this apron of yours?\" If you adorn her, there will be nothing left for her, and if she wears it, then there will be nothing for you. Hearing this, the man sat down until after sitting for a long time he got up (and turned his back) and the Messenger of Allah saw him turning around. You ordered him to be recalled. When he came back, he asked him: \"How much of the Qur'an do you remember?\" He asked: \"Can you recite them?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Go! I have made you its master in exchange for the surahs of the Qur'an that you remember. (Bukhari and Muslim) These words are from Muslim. ) and in a hadith: “Go! I gave her in marriage to you, so teach her some Quran. And in al-Bukhari: \"We have made you its master in exchange for that part of the Qur'an that you remember.\" And in Abu Dawud it is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) that he said: \"How much of the Qur'an do you have memorized?\" ) He said: \"Get up and teach him twenty verses.\" \"."
"834","On the authority of Hazrat Aamir bin Abdullah bin Zubair, he narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Announce the marriage.\""
"835","Hazrat Abu Burda bin Abu Musa narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no marriage without a guardian and guardian.” would not have been held without"
"836","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A woman who marries without the permission of her guardian\" is invalid. Then if the husband has had sexual intercourse with her, the dowry is right for that woman in return for making her private parts lawful. If there is a dispute between the guardians, then the guardian of the one who has no guardian is the guardian of time."
"837","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A widow or a divorced woman should not be married without consulting her.\" And the marriage of a virgin should not be done without taking her permission.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah! How is this (virgin) allowed? He said: “His silence.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"838","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A married woman (for remarriage) has more rights over herself than her guardian.\" And permission will be taken from the virgin and her permission is her silence.” (Muslim) And in a hadith there is: “The guardian has no authority over a widowed woman and an orphan girl should be consulted.”"
"839","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"No woman (by becoming a guardian) can marry another woman, nor can a woman marry herself.\""
"840","Hazrat Nafi narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shaghar. And Shaghar is that a man gives his daughter in marriage to another man on the condition that he will give his daughter in marriage to him and there is no dowry between the two. (Bukhari and Muslim) and Bukhari and Muslim agree with another tradition that this definition of Shaghar is narrated by Nafi."
"841","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that a virgin girl came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and told her that her father had married her while she disliked him. (On hearing this) the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this girl the option (to stay the marriage or annul it). (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah. And this hadith is called Maaloool due to its transmission.)"
"842","Hazrat Hasan narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Hazrat Samura: “A woman who is married by two guardians (to two different people), then this woman will belong to the first husband of them.”"
"843","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A slave who marries without the permission of his owners and his family is an adulterer.\""
"844","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “A mother-in-law, niece, aunt, and niece cannot be brought together (in marriage to a man).” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"845","It is narrated from Hazrat Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A man in ihram can marry himself and not another person.\""
"846","Narrated by Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Hazrat Maimunah, he was in the state of Ihram at that time. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in Muslim, Hazrat Maimunah (RA) has his own statement that when the Prophet (PBUH) married her, she was halal at that time, that is, she was not in the state of Ihram."
"847","On the authority of Hazrat Uqbah bin Aamir, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Of the conditions, the condition by which you have made the private parts of women lawful for you has the most right to be fulfilled.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"848","It was narrated from Hazrat Salama bin Akua that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, allowed Mutah (marriage) for three days in the year of the Battle of Utas, then forbade it. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"849","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ali, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Muttah in the year of Khaybar. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"850","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade sexual intercourse with women and eating domesticated donkeys on the day of Khaibar. (Seven except Abu Dawud have narrated this tradition.)"
"851","Hazrat Rabi bin Sabra narrates from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"I gave you permission to have fun with women.\" Now Allah Ta'ala has made it forbidden until the Day of Judgment, so whoever has one of them (indulgent women), let him leave her and do not take back anything of what you have given her.\""
"852","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed both the one who gives halal and the one for whom halal is given. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Al-Nasa'i and Tirmidhi, and Tirmidhi called it Sahih. And there is also a hadith in this issue from Hazrat Ali, who was mentioned by all four except Al-Nasa'i.)"
"853","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"An adulterer who has committed adultery, marries a woman similar to himself.\""
"854","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, she says that a man divorced his wife three times, then another man married her and divorced her without having intercourse with her. So first the husband wanted to marry her and inquired about it from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and he said: \"No! Until the second husband enjoys it in the same way as the first husband enjoyed it.” (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."
"855","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The Arabs are suffocating to each other and the Mawalis are also suffocating to each other, except for the jula and the barber.\""
"856","It is narrated from Hazrat Fatima bint Qays that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: \"Marry Osama.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"857","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Banu Bayaza! Marry (your daughters) to Abu Hind and marry her also (to one of his dear ones). (Narrated by Abu Dawood and Al-Hakim with a Jaid chain of transmission.)"
"858","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Aisha (RA), she says that when Hazrat Barira (RA) got her freedom, at that time she was given the right to choose her husband (to stay married or not). (Bukhari and Muslim - this is a fragment of a long hadith.) And in Muslim it is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that the husband of Hazrat Berira (RA) was a slave. And there is a tradition from them that he was free. The first tradition is more mature. In Bukhari, the correct saying on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, is that he was a slave."
"859","Hazrat Dahhak bin Firoz Daylami narrated a tradition from his father (Firooz Radi Allahu Anhu) that he says: I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have entered the circle of Islam and I have two sisters in marriage. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Divorce whomever you wish among them.\""
"860","Hazrat Salim narrates from his father that Hazrat Ghilan bin Salama (RA) accepted Islam and had ten wives at that time. All of them accepted Islam along with Ghailan. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Ghailan (may Allah be pleased with him) to choose four of them (and leave the rest)."
"861","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, he says that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent his daughter Hazrat Zainab, after six years, to Abul-Aas because of his first marriage. He did not marry again. (It has been narrated by Ahmad and all four except Nasai and Ahmad and Hakim have declared it to be Sahih.)"
"862","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father and he from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his daughter Hazrat Zaynab back to Abul-Aas with a new marriage. (Tirmidhi said: The hadith narrated by Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, is the best in terms of chain of transmission, but the action is based on the hadith narrated by Amr bin Shuaib.)"
"863","There is a hadith on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that a woman accepted Islam and then got married. Meanwhile, her (first) husband came and said: O Messenger of Allah! I had accepted Islam and he was also aware of my acceptance of Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated her from her second husband and sent her back to her first husband. (Narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah. Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim called it Sahih.)"
"864","Hazrat Zayd bin Ka'b bin Ajrah narrates from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, married a woman named Aaliyah from Banughfar. When she came to him (in private) and he took off his clothes, you saw the whiteness (of the fruit) on his side. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Put on your clothes and go to your house.\" (It was narrated by Al-Hakim and in his chain of transmission Jameel bin Zayd is a narrator who is unknown and there is much disagreement about his teacher.)"
"865","It is narrated from Hazrat Saeed bin Musayb that Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever marries a woman, then has intercourse with her and finds her suffering from leprosy or leprosy, then she (husband) will be given the right to dowry because of her (husband's) companionship with her. And the dowry will be on the part of the husband to the person who cheated him about the woman. (It was narrated by Saeed bin Mansoor, Malik and Ibn Abi Shaiba. And its narrator is Thaqa.) And Saeed (bin Mansoor) narrated the same from Hazrat Ali and added to it that if this woman has the disease of the penis, her husband will be independent. If he has intercourse with a woman, he must pay her mahr in return for making her private parts lawful."
"866","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Saeed bin Musaib that he said: Hazrat Umar (RA) decided about an impotent man that he should be given a grace period of one year. (The narrator of this hadith is Thaqa)."
"867","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever has intercourse with a woman in her company is cursed.”"
"868","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah will not look (with mercy) on a person who commits adultery with a man or has intercourse with a woman in his company.\""
"869","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, he narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who believes in Allah and the Last Day should not persecute his neighbor.\" And accept the will of good concerning women, indeed they are born from a rib. And the most crooked part of the rib is the upper one, so if you try to straighten it, you will break it. And if you leave her (in her state), she will always remain crooked. So accept the will of good in the case of women.\" (Bukhari and Muslim, these words are from Bukhari) And in the tradition of Muslim, it is: \"If you want to gain benefit from this woman, you will be able to benefit from her while she is crooked, and if you try to straighten her, you will break her, and to break her is to divorce her.\""
"870","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who says that we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign. When we returned to Madinah and started going to our respective homes, he said: \"Just stay.\" Night' means entering houses at the time of Isha so that the hair that is disheveled can be combed (etc.) and the one whose husband was absent from the house can clean himself."
"871","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, the person with the worst status in the sight of Allah, the Most High, will be the one who separates from his wife and she (the wife) separates from him.\" Then he walks around revealing her secrets."
"872","Hazrat Hakeem bin Muawiyah narrated from his father: He says that I said: O Messenger of Allah! What right do our wives have over us? He said: \"(That right is) when you eat, feed him and when you wear, wear him too. Don't hit him in the face or abuse him and (in case of displeasure) separate (from him) at home."
"873","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Jews used to say that when a man has sexual intercourse with his wife from behind in the Qibul, the child is born as a virgin. So Allah revealed this verse: Shittum (Women are your fields, so come to your fields as you wish) (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."
"874","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you recites this dua when going to his wife: (I do this work)' God! Keep us away from Shaytan and keep Shaytan away from what You grant us.” So the fact is that if they are destined to have children from this (union), then Shaytan will never be able to harm them.” (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"875","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When a man invites his wife to his bed (for sexual desire) and she refuses to come, and he (husband) spends the night angry, then the angels continue to curse her until morning.\" (Bukhari and Muslim). These words are from Bukhari."
"876","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the one who braids and braids hair (in the head) and also the one who kneads and the mattress.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"877","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Judama bint Wahhab, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I was present with some people in the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was saying: \"I intended to forbid Ghilah (intercourse with a woman during the period of nursing), so I immediately noticed Rome and Persia that they have intercourse with the mothers of their children during the period of nursing, and it does not even harm their children.\""
"878","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri that a man said: O Messenger of Allah! I have a concubine. I separate from her and I don't like her getting pregnant' and I want what men want. The Jews say that to excommunicate a child is to bury him alive. He said: \"The Jews say wrong. If Allah wants to create it, He cannot avert it.”"
"879","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that we used to isolate during the time of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, while the Qur'an was being revealed at that time. If something was forbidden, the Qur'an would have forbidden us from it. (Bukhari and Muslim) And it is in the tradition of Muslim: When this matter reached the Prophet, he did not forbid us from it."
"880","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go to all his wives and take a single bath at the end. (Both Bukhari and Muslim narrated it and these words are Muslim's)."
"881","Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he freed Hazrat Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with him) and declared her freedom as his seal. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"882","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, may God have mercy on him, that he said: I asked Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, how much was the dowry of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: The dowry of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was twelve ounces and one nash for his chaste wives. Then he said: Do you know how much Nish is? He says: I said: No. He said: Half an Oqiya. Thus it became five hundred dirhams. Therefore, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, had this right to dowry for his wives. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"883","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he says that when Hazrat Ali married Fatimah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Give her something.\" Hazrat Ali said: I have nothing. He said: \"Where is that armor of yours?\" (Give it to him.)"
"884","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father and he from his grandfather, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whatever is a condition of dowry, donation or donation, etc. before marriage is the right of a woman.\" And whatever (donation or promise) is after the marriage, then it belongs to him to whom it is given. And the thing due to which a man deserves more respect is his daughter or his sister.” (Narrated by Ahmad and all four except Tirmidhi)."
"885","Hazrat Al-Qamah says that Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud (RA) was asked about a person who married a woman without fixing a dowry for her and did not have intercourse with her until he died. Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud (RA) replied that this woman will get the same dowry as the women of her family. There will be no shortage or excess. And it is also obligatory to spend Eid on it and there is a legacy for it. Hearing this, Hazrat Muaqal bin Sinan Ashjajai (RA) got up and said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) had given a similar decision about one of our women, Birwa bint Washiq. Hazrat Ibn Masood (RA) was very happy about this. (Narrated by Ahmad and four. Tirmidhi called it Sahih and one group called it Hasan.)"
"886","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever gives a woman sata or dates as dowry, he has made it halal (for himself).”"
"887","Hazrat Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi'ah narrated from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the marriage of a woman in exchange for two shoes. (It was narrated by Tirmidhi and declared it Sahih. And Imam Tirmidhi was opposed in declaring it Sahih.)"
"888","On the authority of Hazrat Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, married a man to a woman in exchange for an iron ring. (It was narrated by al-Hakim. And this is a fragment of the long hadith (833) mentioned at the beginning of Kitab al-Nikah.)"
"889","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: \"The dowry is not less than ten dirhams.\""
